IMPORT prelude

-- Building Control Act 1989 (Singapore) -- building without approval and deviating from plans (s 20), occupying a building
-- before completion (s 12), unsafe exterior features such as windows (s 25H with the definitions in s 22A), and unlicensed
-- builders (s 29B).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/BCA1989.txt
-- (amendments to Act 12 of 2020 and Act 15 of 2026).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 33 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository (s 2 by 11; s 42AA, electronic
-- applications, by 7). SCOPED from 377,000 characters to what an owner, occupier or builder meets. Not encoded: plan
-- approval procedure, duties of qualified persons and site supervisors, accredited checkers, retrofitting and
-- accessibility (Parts 3, 3A), environmental sustainability (Part 3B), dangerous buildings and reporting (Part 4),
-- maintenance notices, periodic inspection, the licensing procedure, fixed installation contractors, and the
-- regulations (which prescribe what an "exterior feature" and "insignificant building works" are).
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Building Control Act 1989 -- owners and builders`

§§ `20 -- building without approval, and deviating`

-- s 20(1): commencing or carrying out, or permitting, building works whose plans have not been approved (or deemed
-- approved), or without a required permit -- $200,000 or 2 years, and daily fines.
-- (2): breaching a condition of an approval or permit -- $20,000 or 12 months.
-- (3): anyone "directly concerned" who deviates "in any material way" from approved plans -- $100,000 or 2 years.
-- (4): "(a) it is NOT NECESSARY for the prosecution to prove that an accused KNEW" of the deviation; "(b) it is a defence
-- ... to prove, on a balance of probabilities, that the accused did not know and could not reasonably have known".
-- s 4(1)(d): building works prescribed as "insignificant" are outside Part 2 altogether.
DECLARE Works HAS
    `prescribed as insignificant building works` IS A BOOLEAN
    `plans approved or deemed approved` IS A BOOLEAN
    `deviates materially from the approved plans` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the accused proved they could not reasonably have known of the deviation` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the works` IS A Works
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the works need approval` IF
    NOT `the works`'s `prescribed as insignificant building works`

GIVEN `the works` IS A Works
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `carrying out the works is an offence under section 20(1)` IF
        `the works need approval` `the works`
    AND NOT `the works`'s `plans approved or deemed approved`

GIVEN `the works` IS A Works
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the deviation is an offence under section 20(3)` IF
        `the works`'s `plans approved or deemed approved`
    AND `the works`'s `deviates materially from the approved plans`
    AND NOT `the works`'s `the accused proved they could not reasonably have known of the deviation`

-- In dollars and months.
GIVEN `the works` IS A Works
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    IF `carrying out the works is an offence under section 20(1)` `the works` THEN 200000
    ELSE IF `the deviation is an offence under section 20(3)` `the works` THEN 100000
         ELSE 0

§§ `12 -- occupying a building`

-- s 12(1): a person must not occupy, or permit occupation of, "any building where any building works have been carried out
-- unless the Commissioner ... has issued a certificate of statutory completion". (2): except (a) occupation solely to
-- prevent damage or theft, or (b) under a temporary occupation permit. (4): a TOP "is only PRIMA FACIE evidence that a
-- building is suitable for occupation and is NOT to be taken to be evidence of compliance with the provisions of this Act,
-- the building regulations or any other written law". (6): $20,000 or 6 months, and daily fines.
--
-- (1) applies to "any building where any building works have been carried out" -- read literally, a home that has had
-- approved renovation works needs a fresh certificate before being occupied. Whether "building works" here reaches works
-- to an existing building is not settled by the text.
DECLARE Occupation HAS
    `building works were carried out` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a certificate of statutory completion was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a temporary occupation permit is in force` IS A BOOLEAN
    `occupied solely to prevent damage or theft` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the occupation` IS AN Occupation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupation is lawful` IF
        NOT `the occupation`'s `building works were carried out`
    OR  `the occupation`'s `a certificate of statutory completion was issued`
    OR  `the occupation`'s `a temporary occupation permit is in force`
    OR  `the occupation`'s `occupied solely to prevent damage or theft`

GIVEN `a TOP was granted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the TOP is evidence that the building complies with the Act` IF
    FALSE

§§ `25H -- unsafe exterior features`

-- s 22A: an "exterior feature" is a permanent feature installed on, forming part of or projecting from the roof or exterior,
-- "prescribed by building regulations" (windows among them, by the regulations, not retrieved). The "person responsible" is
-- (a) the OWNER of the premises, or a person in charge of its management and maintenance; (b) for HDB common property, the
-- Town Council or its contractor; for other common property, the owner or managing agent.
-- s 25H(1): a person responsible who "without reasonable excuse, fails to keep or maintain the exterior feature" securely
-- fixed -- $20,000 or 12 months.
-- (2): PRESUMED to have failed if it is proved the feature "has collapsed or fallen" and there is damage or disrepair "not
-- caused by accident or acts of nature".
-- (3): defence -- a defect "caused by materials or work supplied by any person other than the person responsible".
-- (4): not guilty if, "not later than the 7th DAY after a notice alleging" the offence is served, they name by STATUTORY
-- DECLARATION the contractor or agent appointed to maintain it, AND satisfy the court they relied in good faith, after proper
-- inquiry, on that person's expert advice or services.
--
-- When a window falls from a flat, the flat owner is presumed in default. The way out through a contractor closes on day 7.
DECLARE Fall HAS
    `the feature fell or collapsed` IS A BOOLEAN
    `there was damage or disrepair not caused by accident or nature` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the defect came from another's materials or work` IS A BOOLEAN
    `days after the notice the contractor was declared` IS A NUMBER
    `named a contractor by statutory declaration` IS A BOOLEAN
    `relied in good faith after proper inquiry on the contractor` IS A BOOLEAN
    `proved the feature was in fact maintained` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the fall` IS A Fall
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `failure to maintain is presumed` IF
        `the fall`'s `the feature fell or collapsed`
    AND `the fall`'s `there was damage or disrepair not caused by accident or nature`

GIVEN `the fall` IS A Fall
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the contractor route is available` IF
        `the fall`'s `named a contractor by statutory declaration`
    AND `the fall`'s `days after the notice the contractor was declared` AT MOST 7
    AND `the fall`'s `relied in good faith after proper inquiry on the contractor`

GIVEN `the fall` IS A Fall
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person responsible is guilty under section 25H` IF
        `failure to maintain is presumed` `the fall`
    AND NOT `the fall`'s `proved the feature was in fact maintained`
    AND NOT `the fall`'s `the defect came from another's materials or work`
    AND NOT `the contractor route is available` `the fall`

DECLARE Location IS ONE OF
    `a window of a private flat`
    `a feature on HDB common property`
    `a feature on condominium common property`

GIVEN `the location` IS A Location
GIVETH A STRING
`the person responsible` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the location`
    WHEN `a window of a private flat` THEN "the owner of the flat"
    WHEN `a feature on HDB common property` THEN "the Town Council or its contractor"
    WHEN `a feature on condominium common property` THEN "the owner of the common property or its managing agent"

§§ `29B -- unlicensed builders`

-- s 29B(1): no one may hold out as authorised to carry on the business of a general or specialist builder, or use "licensed
-- general builder" or "licensed specialist builder", without the licence. (2): no one may carry on the business of a general
-- builder, or of general and minor specialist building works, or of a specialist builder, without the licence.
GIVEN `carries on a builder's business` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds out as licensed` IS A BOOLEAN, `is licensed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person contravenes section 29B` IF
        (`carries on a builder's business` OR `holds out as licensed`)
    AND NOT `is licensed`
